{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/877402-an-ananasi-in-hengeyokai","id":877402,"title":"An Ananasi in Hengeyokai...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-28T23:51:18-07:00","id":877402,"title":"An Ananasi in Hengeyokai...","content":"Hi everyone, Forum-newb with first post here! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Just some info to give you an idea about my current situation before I get to the actual question:<br /> I play in a Hengeyokai game that we recently started. While this is a new game, I played with this group for quite some time already (Werewolf, something our Storyteller thought of based on cWoD rules, other systems, we're good friends).<br /> We partially chose Hengeyokai to be able to change things up a bit and play a mix of other races instead of just Werewolfs and granted, with everyone taking the chance the group ended up being quite a bit of a &quot;freakshow&quot; in that regard with not a single Hakken in it.<br /> <br /> We are 3 players and the ST provided 2 NPCs to be able to form a mountain Sentai.We've played with NPCs being part of the characters' close surroundings and of the group before and it wasn't a problem.<br /> Our ST was really open with what breeds we could choose (all breedbooks available) so we ended up with a Tengu and a Same-Bito with the NPCs being a Nezumi and a Zhong Lung. I myself always tend to like the more unusual stuff so as he said everything goes wanted to play a Kumo. I mean: when will I possibly have the chance to do so again?<br /> I talked about it with the ST and after some thinking he said as all Kumo have fallen to the Wyrm he'd like the character to be a &quot;standard&quot; Ananasi instead and have me choose one of the Wyld aspects as those are the most likely to assosciate and &quot;fit in&quot; with other breeds. So I built a Kar (Kumoti Myrmidon) and aimed towards the &quot;Leaf&quot; role of the &quot;Sentai to be&quot;, you know, sneaky spy, killer from the shadows, that kinda stuff, while keeping an eye on reflecting on the character-sheet how this guy was able to survive where even other spider-changers would kill him if found. In short I gave him some skills in fighting, stealth, first gifts that help staying save or get out of difficult situations and advantages that aid in that as well.<br /> <br /> The 5 characters now got sent on their first assignment by the court they are part of to prove their worth and end up forming a Sentai.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now a question popped up regarding my character: Totems. We played that the character basically wasn't indoctrinated by elder Ananasi yet as he had his first change only relatively recently (just like all the other chars), learned a few first things from Kumo that picked up the youngling before some elder spider decided he was &quot;not quite right for a Kumo&quot; and to be killed. He managed to narrowly escape long enough for some other Hengeyokai in the area to notice the hunt and intervene, ending up with a young spider-shifter that the Kumo rejected.<br /> <br /> Now as a standard, all Ananasi have Queen Ananasa as totem and are required to follow her rules but my character hasn't been properly instructed as there are no other Ananasi in the court. Now we got thinking: what happens if he doesn't have Ananasa as Totem? Will he be unable to learn any more Ananasi gifts for example? On the other hand the Kumo also don't follow her and can learn the same stuff anyways (and specific Kumo-gifts of course). Also at least the Ananasi believe that all spider-shifters play their role in Ananasa's schemes, knowingly or not.<br /> What happens once the Sentai gets a Totem? One of Ananasa's rules (or at least the rules the Ananasi teach their young) is to not follow the other Totems as they are viewed as &quot;tainted&quot; by the Triad that doesn't work as intended anymore.<br /> <br /> What would you say are our options in playing this? Where are the (hidden or open) problems (and its totally ok if this leads to some problems)?<br /> I already thought about having my character work towards getting a Sentai-Totem that suits him so that the Sentai as a whole may end up with Ananasa as its totem but I'm not sure how to go about this. Also I think for non-Ananasi Queen Ananasa is a pretty costly totem as far as game-rules go (don't know if it would even be possible in this case).<br /> <br /> Of course I will also talk about this some more with my ST and fellow players and I'm sure we'll find a solution but I just wanted to get some more input and ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11694-hexer","name":"Hexer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11694_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T00:07:14-07:00","id":877413,"title":"","content":"I would say even if you have not been 'taught properly', Queen Anasasa would still try bringing you into the fold. <br /> As to the gift things, yes i do agree, if you are NOT totemed to her, its gonna be almost impossible to learn your 'racial' gifts, you would just have to go by general, and auspice type ones..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T00:20:48-07:00","id":877424,"title":"","content":"I've ran/played in more then a few werewolf games (as garou, I think other shifter breeds make great npc's, emphasis on the N) and have always held the belief that while a pack does cleave to their chosen totem each individual still maintains a connection to their tribal totem on some level.<br /> <br /> A child of rat will always be a child of rat, a glasswalker who follows falcon will still have a tie to cockroach because that's what makes him a glasswalker.<br /> <br /> Now they can't call on the benefits that their tribal totem offers but they can still stay in touch.<br /> <br /> TL;DR: let the PC still keep a connection to the queen, it's the spiders birthright that what's makes them weird among the fera. Just don't allow access to her bonuses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T02:19:32-07:00","id":877479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/877402-an-ananasi-in-hengeyokai?p=877424#post877424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've ran/played in more then a few werewolf games (as garou, I think other shifter breeds make great npc's, emphasis on the N) and have always held the belief that while a pack does cleave to their chosen totem each individual still maintains a connection to their tribal totem on some level.<br /> <br /> A child of rat will always be a child of rat, a glasswalker who follows falcon will still have a tie to cockroach because that's what makes him a glasswalker.<br /> <br /> Now they can't call on the benefits that their tribal totem offers but they can still stay in touch.<br /> <br /> TL;DR: let the PC still keep a connection to the queen, it's the spiders birthright that what's makes them weird among the fera. Just don't allow access to her bonuses.</div> </div> </div> </div>hmm true... but wouldn't following a sentai/pack totem go against the rule to &quot;not follow the &quot;totems&quot; of the other Ovid&quot; from the &quot;laws of Ananasa&quot;? Or are these to be viewed more like &quot;laws of the Ananasi&quot; instead? Or does it maybe not contradict it at all if the character chooses to kinda... &quot;play along&quot; with the rules of a sentai-totem as long as it doesn't go against what Ananasa wants?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11694-hexer","name":"Hexer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11694_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T03:07:30-07:00","id":877510,"title":"","content":"You're in a very weird situation. By proclamation of Ananasa The Ananasi are not supposed to meddle with Kumo and the Kumo are not supposed to meddle with Ananasi. For some mysterious reason they function in a way drastically different from the Ananasi and Ananasi are supposed to keep the hell out of Asia. Add to this the fact that the Kumo are enemies of the Hengeyokai (and there are no iffs or butts about it) and you're faced with the fact that your character will be feared and mistrusted. What if you are an infiltrator? How do they even know the difference? Queen Ananasa is not really public knowledge.<br /> <br /> I probably wouldn't have allowed such a character in a Hengeyokai game - especially considering the vagaries of the First Change and the Call. However, you're past that point, and you're probably well aware that you're going to be in trouble with the Hengeyokai and the Kumo with the PC's probably only extending you the benefit of the doubt because &quot;You Seem Trustworhty (TM)&quot;.<br /> <br /> So how to make a lemonade with those lemons? First of all, I'd say that the idea that you do not know about Ananasa and were not trained is a lie. That you have been telling this to everyone, but that both you and your mentor know it... you have heard Ananasa's call and you have been chosen. You do not know what for just yet, but she needs you among the Hengeyokai. You will play the patsy and the misfit and you will learn their ways and methodologies and take them as your own. You will make all the emotional bloodbags care for the little lost spider, but you will serve your mistress first and foremost. The Kumo may try and stop you, because they are not yet privy to Ananasa's grand design, but you know your purpose is just and that her song guides you. I'd keep the mentor as your handler and the person that helps you out logistically, but have him running shadowgames and hiding from the Kumo and the Hengeyokai. The agenda doesn't need to be very clear or even relevant to the plot (but it would be cool if you could get the ST to toss you an occasional secret mission to do in front of the noses of the other PC's).<br /> <br /> As for the totem question, that's easy and works the same as for the Corax and the Nuwisha. You do not get to abandon your totem and its bans, they are an intristic part of who you are and why you are. She will always speak to you, and you will always know joy and horror that she has taken an interest in you. However, Ananasa is clever and she would surely want you to mislead the Food. You will easily join the Sentai and their Totem, you will get the totems perks and bans, but you will still keep Ananasa in your heart and follow her agenda and bans and hear her words. You just won't get any mechanical benefit from Ananasa as a totem.<br /> <br /> If your ST disagrees, nothing stops your crew from being a Wave Sentai.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T03:54:43-07:00","id":877535,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1182_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1182\" data-vbnamecard=\"1182\">Asmodai</a> Thanks a lot! I think that is something I'm going to suggest. I'm sure my ST will come up with something as well as he is one of those guys who knows a lot about the games background and also is very creative. I guess my character already brings enough potential plothooks but why not give the ST more options?<br /> <br /> I am quite aware of course that Kumo will most probably try to kill me on sight and that most if not all Hengeyokai will mistrust me to various degrees.The reason for the Kumo rejecting the char was them noticing those differences between Kumo and Ananasi. This was done &quot;off screen&quot; though so it could be changed. Didn't have any direct influence on the actual game we played or the other characters yet. <br /> <br /> There wasn't much mistrust from the other PCs so far as all of them (including mine) have spent quite some time living in the same place already by now (though not in very close contact with each other) and also there are other things to take care about... like a shark-born Same-Bito who basically needs the other guys as guidance in the world of humans.... or the often absent minded Zhong-Lung and the sometimes cryptic stuff she says when actually paying attention..... or the Tengu who cant keep some of the bird-like behavior reigned in in homid form and has a liking for roadkill.... or the Nezumi who kind of has a big mouth but so far was mostly unable to live up to it... As I said... we're kind of a freakshow in that regard :P<br /> <br /> Actually, there is mention in the breedbook that the Ananasi do send a few of their own as spies to Asia even though they are well aware that those will quite possibly be killed. It's also mentioned in the OOC part that the Kumo have infiltrated the Ananasi by playing on their ignorance of just assuming the Kumo will keep to their own territory.<br /> <br /> I even chose the species my character resembles in Pithus form in a way I think fits with the theme just TOO perfectly not to make use of it: The character is a 20 year old Japanese so I researched spiders common in that country and found that Redback Spiders (originally native to Australia) have been accidentally imported to Japan in 1995 (21 years ago.... go figure) and are now happily living there in the Osaka region despite various tries to annihilate them.<br /> Australia is a pretty bad place for the (relatively few) Ananasi that still live there anyways so I think it wouldn't be THAT far fetched for an Australian Ananasi to be sent to Japan as a spy or whatnot and even siring offspring there (&quot;I could be hunted down and killed if I go there? So what? Not much different to the situation here, eh?&quot;).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11694-hexer","name":"Hexer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11694_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T05:52:20-07:00","id":877604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As I said... we're kind of a freakshow in that regard </div> </div> </div>... pretty much ever PC group ever. Don't worry. It's refreshing to see someone actually investing time and effort to consider the impact and the complexities of a strange character like this one. The point where you introduced the Redback spider's quirky distribution and how conveniently it appeared in Japan is where I really warmed to your concept and the willingness to work it into the setting <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T15:26:08-07:00","id":878166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/877402-an-ananasi-in-hengeyokai?p=877604#post877604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ... pretty much ever PC group ever. Don't worry. It's refreshing to see someone actually investing time and effort to consider the impact and the complexities of a strange character like this one. The point where you introduced the Redback spider's quirky distribution and how conveniently it appeared in Japan is where I really warmed to your concept and the willingness to work it into the setting <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hehe thank you!<br /> I know that its quite the snowflake of a character but if I do something like this I try to make it work. Out of interest and diving deep into the theme I read up a lot about spiders lately and of course also read the breedbook quite a bit. I just wanna make sense playing my characters<br /> <br /> After getting my character into a fight for the first time last session I also thought about if I should offer the group to maybe swap my attributes around and put the main emphasis on social instead of physical to tone down the rather extreme dice pools I get in some things.<br /> I actually was a little shocked myself when I went to spy on something, decided to change into Crawlerling form for that (even though I wouldnt be able to understand human speech, just figured it would be the best to hide), then proceded to realise I was about to roll a handfull of 13(!!) dice for my stealth check now..... something I had not thought about before.<br /> I asked myself if I somehow turned into a powergamer and sure, I knew that it would be good with the high boni on dexterity and dex being an extremely useful stat in cWoD but I did actually want to play that breed because I found it very interesting and unusual (and yea I'm notorious for choosing unusual stuff.<br /> Granted, I'm also the one who can roll a pool of 10 dice and get a result of 1, 1, 2, 2, 3, 3, 4, 4, 6, 9 (I actually took a picture to prove it) so I got told its really not THAT great of a problem for me to have a few dice more to roll <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Ok, off to watch Arachnophobia now <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh btw I have 4 gifts (bought one additional one with freebies) and figured I could actually have learned the 2 that are not Ananasi gifts from Hengeyokai to support the &quot;wasnt really trained&quot;. Open Seal and Mothers Touch should be common enough I guess. Also chose Web Haven and Lost Moments which help explain how he was able to suvive in Asia so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11694,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11694-hexer","user":"Hexer","date":". 04-29-2016, 06:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11694-hexer","name":"Hexer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11694_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T01:22:05-07:00","id":878594,"title":"","content":"Those two are good picks as generalties. Open Seal is one of the best gifts a subtle character can take (though it's not as vital for an Ananasi who can just crawlering through barriers). The cool bit is that you can always heal yourself with blood, so Mother's Touch just makes the other shifters love you more and help them trust you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Oh and remember 8 legged freaks for good measure <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T07:08:04-07:00","id":878702,"title":"","content":"Oh yea,havent watched that one in quite a while.<br /> My only little problem with my gifts is that several of them cost Gnosis and I only have 2 Gnosis haha guess that will be one of the first things to invest XP in.<br /> <br /> Next session is tonight and I already talked to my ST about following Ananasa and all that yesterday evening. Guess he'll think a bit about it and then we'll come up with the solution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11694-hexer","name":"Hexer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11694_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T23:19:33-07:00","id":879934,"title":"","content":"Well that session was fun. We actually killed our main target though we still have to find out what happened to the kinfolk who went missing and why there were traces of other shapeshifters being involved in the whole thing.<br /> <br /> I used Mother's Touch for the first time to patch up the Same Bito a bit (who did a good job of taking as well as causing most of the damage thrown around but somehow seems unable to deal the killing blow to his targets <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) and came up with a little idea:<br /> I will keep a list of who I heal and try to talk them into letting me have some of their blood as a return favor when needed. I'll try not letting the others in the group know about it until its their turn.<br /> <br /> I still haven't told them (at least in game) about all my abilities like being able to change gender (a merit I thought would help to explain how he was able to stay hidden from Kumo and the likes) and while they have seen that he doesn't always look the same in his war-form (merit Lilian Alteration) they haven't investigated about it yet. I guess they might do so though when things get a bit more quiet.<br /> Also I've decided even he himself doesn't yet know about the weird little fact that he actually has an allergy (3 point flaw Allergy) to that special kind of fragrant rosewood just like the Kumo have (the Ananasi usually don't have any equivalent to the Garou's supernatural silver allergy). This could prove interesting as the Same Bito already got a &quot;dagger&quot; made from rosewood from a contact....<br /> <br /> Long story short, I'm having fun and am quite eager to continue playing <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: I have a technical question that I cant find the answer to in the breedbook (though I might have overlooked it): How does an Ananasi's feeding bite feel to the victim?<br /> Do humans bitten to feed blood experience something like the ecstacy of a Vampire's bite? Does it simply hurt?<br /> There is mention in the book of sneaking in in Crawlerling form and feeding without the victim noticing. I also have a fylfot (fetish) that will heal bite-marks or other small puncture wounds as, apparently, that doesn't happen automatic as with a vampires kiss.<br /> so.... what's it like for the victim? Would be good to know before I actually use it first time.<br /> <br /> there is this little paragraph written in-character in the book that I don't know what to make of really:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For another, it's amazing what these little pedipalps can do damage-wise. An as an added bonus, they heal the wounds when they're done makin' 'em. It's a great way to avoid getting accused of being a vampire. </div> </div> </div>huh? they heal the bitewounds? then what do they need that fetish for?<br /> and how does this avoid being accused of being a vampire? vampire bites also just heal, don't they??<br /> what does this little piece try to tell us?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11694,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11694-hexer","user":"Hexer","date":". 05-02-2016, 07:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11694-hexer","name":"Hexer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11694_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T05:23:54-07:00","id":880075,"title":"","content":"I'm going to have to check, but I'm pretty sure the idea is that the pedipalps daw blood and close the wound. I always went for Vampire-like ecstasy, simply because some of the freaky unwanted sexuality should be preserved, but it could as well work just like shock and horror. I do remember the flyfoot you mentioned, and that does make the whole thing a bit more confusing.<br /> <br /> I'll check the books when I get home and get back to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T05:28:49-07:00","id":880082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/877402-an-ananasi-in-hengeyokai?p=880075#post880075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to have to check, but I'm pretty sure the idea is that the pedipalps daw blood and close the wound. I always went for Vampire-like ecstasy, simply because some of the freaky unwanted sexuality should be preserved, but it could as well work just like shock and horror. I do remember the flyfoot you mentioned, and that does make the whole thing a bit more confusing.<br /> <br /> I'll check the books when I get home and get back to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be great, thanks! I was looking too, but couldn't find it. At character creation I guess I just saw the Fylfot and went like &quot;oh so the bite doesn't heal supernaturally like a Vampires, in this case it would be great to have this!&quot; *notes down on character-sheet* and then didn't think further about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11694-hexer","name":"Hexer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11694_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T01:51:13-07:00","id":880813,"title":"","content":"Kumo can join the beast courts, 274 CB20 Each Kumo has to make a conscious choice to serve the wyrm and while this may be coerced some Kumo do balk and run when the option is given. Generally the Emerald Courts put ALOT of effort into making sure this isn't an elaborate ruse when the Spider shows up and they have to deal with every other Kumo trying to kill them but its not unknown or impossible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T02:23:54-07:00","id":880823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/877402-an-ananasi-in-hengeyokai?p=880813#post880813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kumo can join the beast courts, 274 CB20 Each Kumo has to make a conscious choice to serve the wyrm and while this may be coerced some Kumo do balk and run when the option is given. Generally the Emerald Courts put ALOT of effort into making sure this isn't an elaborate ruse when the Spider shows up and they have to deal with every other Kumo trying to kill them but its not unknown or impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>... that's new :P. I really need to read that damn book back to back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T05:18:06-07:00","id":880884,"title":"","content":"anyone got any insights on the question regarding an Ananasi's feeding bite?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11694-hexer","name":"Hexer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11694_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T05:38:24-07:00","id":880894,"title":"","content":"I checked the old CB book, the new CB book and the W20 book to little help. That's what I had in PDF. I'll have to go through the breedbook when I'm home. Sorry, was running Mage last night so didn't get to sit down with it in peace.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T05:54:58-07:00","id":880906,"title":"","content":"No prob. I'm just trying to find something within the next 2 days if possible as we will play again then and I will likely want to use this for the first time then. I'm still scanning the Breedbook for anything I can find but haven't really found anything yet.<br /> There is one scene where one of the young Ananasi that are taught is allowed to feed off a captured Nuwisha but it only says how she feeds, not if the Nuwisha (who is already a drooling mess at this point after having seen an avatar of Ananasa) expriences pain or pleasure or whatever from the bite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11694-hexer","name":"Hexer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11694_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T11:25:59-07:00","id":881114,"title":"","content":"I suggest going with whatever is most fun and interesting, there, honestly. If the book doesn't provide you an answer before the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T16:19:56-07:00","id":881339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/877402-an-ananasi-in-hengeyokai?p=880906#post880906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No prob. I'm just trying to find something within the next 2 days if possible as we will play again then and I will likely want to use this for the first time then. I'm still scanning the Breedbook for anything I can find but haven't really found anything yet.<br /> There is one scene where one of the young Ananasi that are taught is allowed to feed off a captured Nuwisha but it only says how she feeds, not if the Nuwisha (who is already a drooling mess at this point after having seen an avatar of Ananasa) expriences pain or pleasure or whatever from the bite.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've gone through the whole book. From what I can infer from in the &quot;education&quot; chapter, you can draw blood while in Crawlering and the wounds will heal. It's slightly less clear on Homid, but it says that anything done by your pedipalps (note, not your fangs, only your pedipalps!) will close once you're done to help hide what you are. As you have pedipalps even in homid, you're pretty much sold on cleaning up your own messes.<br /> <br /> I'd assume the Fylfot is there for exotic uses - note that it speaks that its maker is a blood connoisseur - so I assume it's there to hide exotic way to get and drink blood, as it hides a lot of small sharp objects you might want to use - razors, stilletos, needles, your own fangs....<br /> <br /> Page 42. speaks of manipulating, controlling and putting fear into your victims, which probably implies that there is little of the ecstasy that the Vampire's kiss offers. It also is rather informative that you don't get a Herd option (not that Ananasi would ever want one <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />). However, considering that Ananasi have a thing for poisons and chemicals, and that they can feed of sleeping people, one would assume they can excrete a mild anaesthetic along with their blood drawing. This would help hide their feeding and the fact that a bite wouldn't be as horribly painful as it should be, possibly feeling like slight pricking - it's surely not enough to wake a sleeping person up, and I'm assuming that someone who is afraid, cajoled, seduced and otherwise distracted might not realise what exactly happened.<br /> <br /> Hope this helps. I'm curious where you're planning to go with the character later on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T22:11:50-07:00","id":881503,"title":"","content":"The few times in game i have seen Ananasi pop up the Dm didn't run their bites like vampires 'ecstasy. but for crawlerling form, its just like a bug bite. I have woken up Many a times and found bug bits on me (even 2 spider bites before, lucky they were not poisonous or brown recluses@!!) and don't remember getting bit in the night.. So to me it would seem its not noticed if they are asleep.<br /> Bigger issue i see, is how many 'blood points' can you draw when IN crawlering form?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T00:29:43-07:00","id":881573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/877402-an-ananasi-in-hengeyokai?p=881503#post881503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bigger issue i see, is how many 'blood points' can you draw when IN crawlering form?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's easy. One per Master Spider. There's hardly much more room in the Master Spiders then that.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T00:47:38-07:00","id":881578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/877402-an-ananasi-in-hengeyokai?p=881339#post881339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've gone through the whole book. From what I can infer from in the &quot;education&quot; chapter, you can draw blood while in Crawlering and the wounds will heal. It's slightly less clear on Homid, but it says that anything done by your pedipalps (note, not your fangs, only your pedipalps!) will close once you're done to help hide what you are. As you have pedipalps even in homid, you're pretty much sold on cleaning up your own messes.</div> </div> </div> </div>hmmm how is there a difference made between &quot;using your pedipalps&quot; and &quot;using your fangs&quot;? I mean pedipalps are those little appendages that carry a spiders &quot;fangs&quot;. They cant really inflict any wounds on their own if you exclude the fangs from the consideration. So I would guess if wounds inflicted by means of the pedipalps heal after feeding then that means bite-wounds.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd assume the Fylfot is there for exotic uses - note that it speaks that its maker is a blood connoisseur - so I assume it's there to hide exotic way to get and drink blood, as it hides a lot of small sharp objects you might want to use - razors, stilletos, needles, your own fangs.... </div> </div> </div>its true that the Fylfot will work to hide other small puncture wounds as well, maybe I just got confused by the wording of the description and the picture that shows the guy biting his victim through it... meh<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Page 42. speaks of manipulating, controlling and putting fear into your victims, which probably implies that there is little of the ecstasy that the Vampire's kiss offers. It also is rather informative that you don't get a Herd option (not that Ananasi would ever want one <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />). However, considering that Ananasi have a thing for poisons and chemicals, and that they can feed of sleeping people, one would assume they can excrete a mild anaesthetic along with their blood drawing. This would help hide their feeding and the fact that a bite wouldn't be as horribly painful as it should be, possibly feeling like slight pricking - it's surely not enough to wake a sleeping person up, and I'm assuming that someone who is afraid, cajoled, seduced and otherwise distracted might not realise what exactly happened. </div> </div> </div>Well it speaks of keeping them under control by fear <b>or other means. </b>It also goes on about &quot;the less they know, the better&quot; which I would read as advice to not let them know you are something other than a mere human. There also is &quot;Use your wiles, and your skills to draw them in, and keep them returning for the promise of more;...&quot; which sounds like it would be great advice to vampires just as well as Ananasi and seems to imply there is something that makes it very worthwile for the victims to come back for more.<br /> <br /> Well I guess in the end I will have to talk to my ST to clear this up.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11694-hexer","name":"Hexer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11694_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T00:50:16-07:00","id":881581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/877402-an-ananasi-in-hengeyokai?p=881573#post881573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's easy. One per Master Spider. There's hardly much more room in the Master Spiders then that.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>that would mean 10 points of blood if you use 10 &quot;leader&quot; spiders (which is the maximum number without getting mali on stuff from splitting up your consciousness to much) which is what the book describes as the maximum amount you can get out of a human before he/she is sucked dry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11694-hexer","name":"Hexer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11694_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T22:27:54-07:00","id":883497,"title":"","content":"Ok, so my ST took the bit of text on page 68 of the breedbook to mean that only crawlerling bites heal over and yea... you don't really notice bug-bites in the night. This also means that the Fetish is not &quot;useless&quot; as I still need it to cover up feeding in homid form and we also went with Ananasi excreting a mild anesthetic while biting so you can hide the fact of what you're actually doing there in a lot of situations. I'm quite happy with that solution.<br /> <br /> In other news, we returned from our first mission, there was some hearing, discussing and judging between us and the higher ups of the court and now I ended up becoming the Sentais Lantern and the Nezumi as Leaf. There was some part OOC motivation behind the swap as its not that great to have an NPC with a leading role for the player group but it also made sense to do it IC even though we realize that it means we will face more problems when dealing with other Hengeyokai.<br /> We are now in the Umbra and searching for a Totem. We might end up with Mongoose but had to stop somewhat early because of (OOC) work the next day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11694-hexer","name":"Hexer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11694_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T01:53:55-07:00","id":894614,"title":"","content":"We found something else weird in the Ananasi Breedbook when re-reading the forms descriptions. There on page 65 in the description of the Pithus (giant spider) form there is this part:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But of of the biggest advantages to this form comes from the fact that spiders are... well, hydraulic in nature. Their muscles don't work in the same way, and neither does their circulatory system. Spiders can shift the blood in their bodies, and that allows them to increase the amount of strength they have substantially. Damh\u00e0n can do the same thing, but it takes more out of us. Yes, we can increase our strength very efficiently, but we will have to replenish our blood if we do it too often. I personally don't have a problem with that; I like the taste of blood. </div> </div> </div>Whats this supposed to be about?<br /> It kinda makes it sound like Ananasi could use blood to increase strength in Pithus form (like a Vampire would) but its not mentioned in the rules.<br /> Is it just a fluffy explanation for why the Pithus form has a higher strength bonus than the other forms? Then why does it talk about having to replenish blood?<br /> Is it a hint at the gift that lets you pump blood points into strength? Then why is it described as universal and only for the Pithus form?<br /> <br /> Didn't really make a lot of sense to us...<br /> <br /> EDIT: oh and in other news, we have a Totem now: Bear (the Asian version). Which is somewhat weird for me because it means (among other things) that every time a member of the sentai takes a first wound during a fight, everyone else in the sentai will feel it and get 2 temporary rage... which includes me. Happened one time so far and I rolled rage to see if it would have any weird effects, but it didn't.<br /> It also means that we are not allowed to attack any other Hengeyokai with natural weapons (Fangs, Claws, ...). Thing is, that &quot;other Hengeyokai&quot; in Bears mind includes Kumo so this might cause problems for me.<br /> Will have to re-read if Ananasi view Kumo as just mislead brethren or a whole other breed or something because its a kind of unwritten law that Ananasi don't use weapons when fighting each other, only cunning and what the queen gave to them naturally which would reduce my options to cunning in conflict with Kumo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11694,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11694-hexer","user":"Hexer","date":". 05-20-2016, 05:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11694-hexer","name":"Hexer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11694_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T02:09:07-07:00","id":894617,"title":"","content":"Look at the rank 4 gift hydraulic strength.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T02:14:27-07:00","id":894618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/877402-an-ananasi-in-hengeyokai?p=894617#post894617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look at the rank 4 gift hydraulic strength.</div> </div> </div> </div>yea I know, we also thought it might be a reference to that but then, why is it made sound as if it was a universal ability? I mean, a rank 4 gift is pretty high, I don't think THAT many Ananasi would have that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11694-hexer","name":"Hexer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11694_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T02:20:35-07:00","id":894623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/877402-an-ananasi-in-hengeyokai?p=894618#post894618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> yea I know, we also thought it might be a reference to that but then, why is it made sound as if it was a universal ability? I mean, a rank 4 gift is pretty high, I don't think THAT many Ananasi would have that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kinda redundant if you can do it normally and then have a gift that does the same thing? The fluff you quoted said that yes can do the same thing but it costs more. Operative term can, not we all can or only I can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T02:22:02-07:00","id":894624,"title":"","content":"hmm true. I'm just gonna take it to mean that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11694-hexer","name":"Hexer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11694_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T02:30:15-07:00","id":894629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/877402-an-ananasi-in-hengeyokai?p=894614#post894614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: oh and in other news, we have a Totem now: Bear (the Asian version). Which is somewhat weird for me because it means (among other things) that every time a member of the sentai takes a first wound during a fight, everyone else in the sentai will feel it and get 2 temporary rage... which includes me. Happened one time so far and I rolled rage to see if it would have any weird effects, but it didn't.<br /> It also means that we are not allowed to attack any other Hengeyokai with natural weapons (Fangs, Claws, ...). Thing is, that &quot;other Hengeyokai&quot; in Bears mind includes Kumo so this might cause problems for me.<br /> Will have to re-read if Ananasi view Kumo as just mislead brethren or a whole other breed or something because its a kind of unwritten law that Ananasi don't use weapons when fighting each other, only cunning and what the queen gave to them naturally which would reduce my options to cunning in conflict with Kumo.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't have Rage and therefore cannot gain Rage points, so that's not how it works. As for the ban, I'm pretty sure it doesn't qualify Kumo. They qualify as enemies of all the courts. Mind you, I wouldn't extend the ban to you either - so if another follower of bear wanted to murder you, they probably could with no ill effects.<br /> <br /> The idea about not using weapon comes from the desire not to actually murder the other Ananasi. If you fight you don't aim to kill the other, because that's Ananasa's purview and choice, and she might have designs for the person you wanted to kill. With the Kumo, all bets are off since they're batshit insane. Just consider what they do with their Metis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T02:44:09-07:00","id":894634,"title":"","content":"hmmmm well Bear (our ST) was pretty explicit about Kumo being included as he is a very &quot;old-fashioned&quot; Totem and all... *shrugs* I don't care much either way to be honest. It just effects how I will have to go about facing off against a Kumo should I ever get into that situation (I might though, already had a vision of being killed by a Kumo).<br /> <br /> Actually I seem to remember from the breed book that its not really a big thing for Ananasi to kill each other as long as they don't try to go on a rampage killing of brethren &quot;just because&quot;. Its just a matter of: If you are gonna fight each other, use what the mother queen gave you to fight with, not some artificial tools!<br /> Its just in the holy places that killing other Ananasi is forbidden.<br /> <br /> EDIT: ah, here it is:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><i>Ban:</i> Bear forbids his children to use their natural weaponry against other hengeyokai, even Kumo, lest any more of the Mother's Children perish. Bear does not prohibit the use of Gifts or weaponry against those who oppose the Emerald Mother of Her creatures.</span> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11694,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11694-hexer","user":"Hexer","date":". 05-20-2016, 05:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11694-hexer","name":"Hexer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11694_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T02:55:52-07:00","id":894636,"title":"","content":"Well there is nothing in that ban that precludes maiming your opponents, I remember an old Shaw brothers film &quot;8 diagram pole fighter&quot; in it the monks train with wooden wolf shaped dummies and practice knocking the teeth out. Which comes in handy later in the film against the big villains gang.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T03:07:51-07:00","id":894641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/877402-an-ananasi-in-hengeyokai?p=894636#post894636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well there is nothing in that ban that precludes maiming your opponents, I remember an old Shaw brothers film &quot;8 diagram pole fighter&quot; in it the monks train with wooden wolf shaped dummies and practice knocking the teeth out. Which comes in handy later in the film against the big villains gang.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might be a language-barrier thing but I'd read it as quite clear with &quot;to use their natural weaponry&quot;.<br /> It was interpreted though that it would be fine to use fists and whatnot, just not Claws and Teeth and whatever else causes aggravated damage and can easily kill a shifter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11694-hexer","name":"Hexer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11694_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T03:11:08-07:00","id":894644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/877402-an-ananasi-in-hengeyokai?p=894641#post894641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It might be a language-barrier thing but I'd read it as quite clear with &amp;quot;to use their natural weaponry&amp;quot;.<br /> It was interpreted though that it would be fine to use fists and whatnot, just not Claws and Teeth and whatever else causes aggravated damage and can easily kill a shifter.</div> </div> </div> </div>8 diagram pole fighters use poles......","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T03:35:21-07:00","id":894650,"title":"","content":"oh that's what you meant. in this case I agree!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11694-hexer","name":"Hexer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11694_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T04:14:38-07:00","id":894655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/877402-an-ananasi-in-hengeyokai?p=894634#post894634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">hmmmm well Bear (our ST) was pretty explicit about Kumo being included as he is a very &quot;old-fashioned&quot; Totem and all... *shrugs* I don't care much either way to be honest. It just effects how I will have to go about facing off against a Kumo should I ever get into that situation (I might though, already had a vision of being killed by a Kumo).</div> </div> </div> </div>If you do not have a Rage stat I don't see how you could ever gain or use Rage. The implications of this are quite staggering as there are ways to actually join kinfolk into packs. Imagine the possibility of 10 kinfolk with Rage based bonus actions as a part of the pack under the same totem as the pack leading them into battle. So, no, I'd pretty vehemently oppose any idea of allowing the rule to cross that boundary. It gets even worse once you start crossing things over.<br /> <br /> When Bear was written he did not actually consider the possibility of Ananasi/Kumo (or Nuwisha) in a pack, as the original Hengeyokai book had the Kumo as ALWAYS EVIL (TM).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><i>Ban:</i> Bear forbids his children to use their natural weaponry against other hengeyokai, even Kumo, lest any more of the Mother's Children perish. Bear does not prohibit the use of Gifts or weaponry against those who oppose the Emerald Mother of Her creatures.</span> </div> </div> </div>Aha. Don't remember that as I don't really have the books at hand at work, but Bear's ban is downright silly. And that expressly allows you to kill people with Fetishes and weapons doing aggravated damage. I'd sooner term it as Bear forbidding you from killing any shifters. (it's less explicit about kneecaps and general condition you survive in <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T04:32:25-07:00","id":894658,"title":"","content":"Well I was also kinda surprised the rage thing should work on me. I mean personally I would be ok with it not working for my character at all. I still have blood after all (even though Rage can be more powerful in a fight except for special uses that other shifters don't get). I think I'll ask my ST again and see how we end up doing it. It would basically just mean I have to be a little more carefull still in a fight as I have more problems with healing damage than other shifters. I also have higher dodge and block dice-pools than most of them though so there's that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11694-hexer","name":"Hexer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11694_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}